\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Wheeled-legged M1, real rolling traverses. Left: estimated base paths against the vendor odometry (thick olive = the straight-rolling runs used for testing). Right: the heading-independent metric --- fraction of the driven path length recovered. The rolling-contact model recovers essentially all of it; the fixed-foot model recovers almost none, because it treats a continuously rolling robot as near-stationary.}}{7}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
